      <section class="section" style="background:var(--white);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Must-See Sights</span><h2 class="display-h2">Iconic experiences in Shanghai</h2></div><div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);"><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>The Bund</h3><p>Shanghai's iconic waterfront — walk at blue hour when the Pudong skyline lights up across the Huangpu River.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Yu Garden & Old Town</h3><p>A 400-year-old classical garden surrounded by teahouses, silk shops and xiaolongbao restaurants.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>French Concession</h3><p>Tree-lined streets, hidden bars, indie boutiques and the city's best brunch spots.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Shanghai Tower</h3><p>The world's second-tallest building — ride to the 118th floor for a 546 m panoramic view.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Nanjing Road</h3><p>One of the world's busiest shopping streets — a neon ribbon from the Bund to People's Square.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Zhujiajiao</h3><p>An ancient water town of stone bridges and canals on the city's fringe — a calm counterpoint to the towers.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Shanghai on a Plate"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-copy reveal"><span class="eyebrow">Food Capital</span><h2 class="display-h2">Shanghai on a Plate</h2><p>Shanghainese cuisine (benbang) is sweet, savoury and refined — the opposite of inland heat. The icon is xiaolongbao, soup dumplings lifted from a bamboo steamer in a single practised pinch. Our food walks pair the dumpling trail with the city's best shengjian and braised pork.</p><p>From street-side steamers to Michelin tables, Shanghai lets you taste China's full range without leaving the metro.</p><ul class="tour-highlights" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px;"><li><strong>Xiaolongbao</strong> — delicate soup dumplings, a Shanghainese rite of passage</li><li><strong>Shengjian bao</strong> — pan-fried buns with a crisp base and juicy centre</li><li><strong>Hong shao rou</strong> — glossy, sweet, slow-cooked braised pork belly</li><li><strong>Scallion-oil noodles</strong> — humble but deeply addictive</li><li><strong>Hairy crab (dazha xie)</strong> — autumn's luxury, eaten with ginger vinegar</li></ul></div><div class="split-media reveal reveal-d1"><img src="assets/img/shanghai-food.jpg" alt="Shanghai xiaolongbao" /><div class="seal-stamp" aria-hidden="true">本<br/>帮</div></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "A perfect 4-day journey"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--paper-deep);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Sample Itinerary</span><h2 class="display-h2">A perfect 4-day journey</h2><p>Every journey we design is tailor-made — this is a favourite starting point.</p></div><div class="steps-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:22px;"><div class="step reveal"><span class="step-num">01</span><h3>Arrival &amp; The Bund</h3><p>Private transfer, then The Bund at blue hour and a stroll down Nanjing Road as the neon switches on.</p></div><div class="step reveal reveal-d1"><span class="step-num">02</span><h3>Old &amp; French</h3><p>Yu Garden and the Old Town in the morning, then the French Concession on foot and Xintiandi for dinner.</p></div><div class="step reveal reveal-d2"><span class="step-num">03</span><h3>Up &amp; Away</h3><p>Shanghai Tower for the 546 m view, the Shanghai Museum's jade and calligraphy, then a Maglev thrill to Pudong.</p></div><div class="step reveal reveal-d3"><span class="step-num">04</span><h3>Water Town Farewell</h3><p>A morning in Zhujiajiao's canals, last shopping on Nanjing Road, and a private transfer to the airport.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Shanghai after dark"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-media reveal"><img src="assets/img/shanghai-night.jpg" alt="The Bund Shanghai at night" /></div><div class="split-copy reveal reveal-d1"><span class="eyebrow">Night Views</span><h2 class="display-h2">Shanghai after dark</h2><p>After dark, Shanghai is the most glamorous city in China. The Bund's heritage façades glow amber while Pudong's towers pulse with colour across the river; river cruises slide beneath the lit bridges; and the French Concession's hidden bars hum with jazz.</p><ul class="tour-highlights" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px;"><li>The Bund & Pudong light show across the Huangpu River</li><li>Evening river cruise past the illuminated skyline</li><li>French Concession hidden jazz bars and cocktail lounges</li><li>Xintiandi rooftop dining and people-watching</li></ul></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Beyond the city"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--white);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Nearby Escapes</span><h2 class="display-h2">Beyond the city</h2></div><div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);"><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Suzhou</h3><p>The 'Venice of the East' — classical scholar gardens and canals, just 30 minutes by high-speed train.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M3 18l6-8 4 5 3-4 5 7z"/><path d="M3 21h18"/></svg></div><h3>Hangzhou</h3><p>West Lake and terraced tea hills — China's most poetic landscape, 1 h by rail and an easy day trip.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 18h16M6 18V8l6-4 6 4v10"/><path d="M10 18v-4h4v4"/></svg></div><h3>Wuzhen</h3><p>A preserved water town of stone bridges and lanterns — a photographer's dusk, an hour from the centre.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Good to know"
    html: |
      <section class="commit-band section"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal" style="margin-bottom:20px;"><span class="eyebrow centered">Travel Tips</span><h2 class="display-h2">Good to know before you go</h2></div><div class="commit-grid" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;"><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Getting around</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">The metro is world-class, cheap and English-signposted; the Maglev is the fastest (and most fun) airport run on earth.</p></div></div><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Best viewpoints</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">The classic Bund shot is from the Pudong (east) riverbank at Binjiang, or from a dusk cruise on the river itself.</p></div></div><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Seasons</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">Spring brings cherry blossoms; autumn is crisp and clear. Summers are hot and humid — plan indoor museums for midday.</p></div></div><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Booking ahead</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">Top-floor tower tickets and the best xiaolongbao restaurants sell out — we reserve both so you skip the queue.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
